    "rationale": "The undiluted readings stay flat at about 1.22–1.26 from 6 h to 18 h. Before that, growth was steady, with 2.3–2.5x increases per hour up to 5 h, and then it stopped abruptly. That pattern fits a reader that stops responding at high density, rather than a culture that gradually runs out of nutrients. One 10x dilution of the 18 h aliquot read 0.1325, which corresponds to about 1.33 OD. The undiluted 18 h reading was 1.209, so the diluted sample implies about 10% more biomass. This was a single replicate with no budget left, so the evidence is moderate and not conclusive. The direction still favours the undiluted readings underestimating biomass."
